    {
      "id": 17,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"synthesis\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research input throughput and storage using A's flat implementation bbf53e3df0dd4040 as the simple control. Replace both cin and per-element scanf with one buffered fread integer reader, supporting whitespace, optional signs, INT_MIN, tokens crossing buffer boundaries and EOF without a trailing newline. First isolate the parser change; then compare the existing raw-row ring 906333de13ce4fe7 against flat storage with identical parsing. Investigate eliminating initialization of storage that is fully overwritten before use. Preserve initialized column accumulators and correct ring warm-up. Deliver a standalone measured program and clearly identify parser versus layout effects.\",\"B\":\"Research reusable ARM64 SIMD kernels from c8994f068c464610, retaining its scalar fallback. Adapt the four-delta inclusive scan to A/C's horizontal scan over 64-bit column sums: retain the carry, evaluate every window and accumulate maxima without materializing a separate horizontal-sums array. These inputs are already 64-bit; do not reuse the donor's 32-bit widening loads or narrow them. Use supported 64-bit compare/select operations for vector maxima and correct scalar tails. Also examine independent entering/exiting column updates with widening before subtraction. Compare against the existing horizontal-history implementation; do not mark a dependent recurrence as an independent SIMD loop.\",\"C\":\"Research whether the reported advantage of cooperative band seeding in 69e8a257994d4eba is reproducible over serial A and independent-band d930a3faeae74923. Keep contiguous row bands, private rolling columns, one parallel region and a final maximum reduction. Refine worker/seeding selection using candidate-row count M=N-S+1, useful scan work, duplicated initialization N*T*S, cooperative prefix reads and synchronization cost—not matrix area alone. Respect the available OpenMP team, the four-core target and actual team size; retain a serial fallback. Avoid per-row barriers and shared hot-loop maxima. Deliver measured evidence distinguishing parallel scanning from seed preparation benefits.\",\"G\":\"Integrate complete child programs, not overlapping whole-file patches or the truncated C diff. Preserve 69e8a257994d4eba as the reported-best control and A's flat implementation as the simplicity control. Prioritize measured comparisons of A's parser with serial A and cooperative C, then add B's compatible 64-bit kernels to the better foundation. Keep B's horizontal-history design as an alternative rather than combining incompatible storage schemes. Revalidate and measure each actual combination with the unchanged harness and within existing budgets; parser, SIMD and threading gains need not add. Audit negative maxima, wide intermediates, S=1, S=N-1, ring initialization, SIMD tails and reduced OpenMP teams. Retain the best validated measured program, even if an unchanged donor beats every integration.\",\"analysis\":\"The relevant task is Problem B: maximum S-by-S matrix sum. The baseline repeatedly scans window edges; all six admissible programs replace that work with O(N²) rolling sums. Reported means fall from 130.22 ms to 54.18–55.71 ms, approximately 2.34–2.40× faster. Cooperative C is nominally fastest, but its lead over simple flat A is only about 1.6%; candidate variability and phase timings are unavailable. Every donor retains per-integer scanf, making input parsing a promising shared bottleneck hypothesis, not an established diagnosis. Research should separate input/storage, SIMD and parallelization effects. Every valid input must remain correct: the 32-bit result guarantee does not bound intermediate sums, so retain signed 64-bit accumulation and widen before subtraction. Keep tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target and permissions unchanged; never specialize to benchmark values.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"916936c4708d6adb544f9c4261b5f3bb0a622171171eaf96e18bf428cea2565a\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research input throughput and storage using A's flat implementation bbf53e3df0dd4040 as the simple control. Replace both cin and per-element scanf with one buffered fread integer reader, supporting whitespace, optional signs, INT_MIN, tokens crossing buffer boundaries and EOF without a trailing newline. First isolate the parser change; then compare the existing raw-row ring 906333de13ce4fe7 against flat storage with identical parsing. Investigate eliminating initialization of storage that is fully overwritten before use. Preserve initialized column accumulators and correct ring warm-up. Deliver a standalone measured program and clearly identify parser versus layout effects.\",\"B\":\"Research reusable ARM64 SIMD kernels from c8994f068c464610, retaining its scalar fallback. Adapt the four-delta inclusive scan to A/C's horizontal scan over 64-bit column sums: retain the carry, evaluate every window and accumulate maxima without materializing a separate horizontal-sums array. These inputs are already 64-bit; do not reuse the donor's 32-bit widening loads or narrow them. Use supported 64-bit compare/select operations for vector maxima and correct scalar tails. Also examine independent entering/exiting column updates with widening before subtraction. Compare against the existing horizontal-history implementation; do not mark a dependent recurrence as an independent SIMD loop.\",\"C\":\"Research whether the reported advantage of cooperative band seeding in 69e8a257994d4eba is reproducible over serial A and independent-band d930a3faeae74923. Keep contiguous row bands, private rolling columns, one parallel region and a final maximum reduction. Refine worker/seeding selection using candidate-row count M=N-S+1, useful scan work, duplicated initialization N*T*S, cooperative prefix reads and synchronization cost—not matrix area alone. Respect the available OpenMP team, the four-core target and actual team size; retain a serial fallback. Avoid per-row barriers and shared hot-loop maxima. Deliver measured evidence distinguishing parallel scanning from seed preparation benefits.\",\"G\":\"Integrate complete child programs, not overlapping whole-file patches or the truncated C diff. Preserve 69e8a257994d4eba as the reported-best control and A's flat implementation as the simplicity control. Prioritize measured comparisons of A's parser with serial A and cooperative C, then add B's compatible 64-bit kernels to the better foundation. Keep B's horizontal-history design as an alternative rather than combining incompatible storage schemes. Revalidate and measure each actual combination with the unchanged harness and within existing budgets; parser, SIMD and threading gains need not add. Audit negative maxima, wide intermediates, S=1, S=N-1, ring initialization, SIMD tails and reduced OpenMP teams. Retain the best validated measured program, even if an unchanged donor beats every integration.\",\"analysis\":\"The relevant task is Problem B: maximum S-by-S matrix sum. The baseline repeatedly scans window edges; all six admissible programs replace that work with O(N²) rolling sums. Reported means fall from 130.22 ms to 54.18–55.71 ms, approximately 2.34–2.40× faster. Cooperative C is nominally fastest, but its lead over simple flat A is only about 1.6%; candidate variability and phase timings are unavailable. Every donor retains per-integer scanf, making input parsing a promising shared bottleneck hypothesis, not an established diagnosis. Research should separate input/storage, SIMD and parallelization effects. Every valid input must remain correct: the 32-bit result guarantee does not bound intermediate sums, so retain signed 64-bit accumulation and widen before subtraction. Keep tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target and permissions unchanged; never specialize to benchmark values.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"nonce\":\"f892719daca94011a93d325b821830e7\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"xhigh\",\"request_sha256\":\"916936c4708d6adb544f9c4261b5f3bb0a622171171eaf96e18bf428cea2565a\",\"session_id\":\"2bd8b683b45b41c8b48ec38708f46bab\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"e1d9264a6fd33554544ee2b13ef3d035e16811c585d400b9f578866859212230\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":21577,\"output_tokens\":3367,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":2588}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"xhigh\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":24944,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
